43284f207bff35eba24617fd4245a69d439ed151d09eed564813f9d72fb.png)\n\nThe *distance* between the number $-3$ and $0$ is known as the **absolute value** of $-3.$ We write it as\n\n$$\n|-3| = {\\color{red}3}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, $|\\,2\\,|$, the absolute value of the number $2$, is the distance between $2$ and $0$:\n\n![](images/f4/f44fcd05fb0932083d48c8b11892247d8de8fbc46ccf7186fb12843702181aea.png)\n\nWe write $|\\,2\\,| = {\\color{red}2}.$\n\nSo, the absolute value simply \n\n- *removes the minus sign*, if the number is negative, or\n\n- does nothing, if the number is non-negative.\n\nSometimes, we can be asked to evaluate an expression involving the absolute value function, like $|x +1| + 5$ when $x=-3.$ In this case, we evaluate the expression inside the absolute value before simplifying the rest of the expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x+1|+5 & = \\\\ |(-3)+1|+5 & = \\\\ |-2|+5 & = \\\\ 2+5 & = \\\\ 7 & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056066 #edb/ref 1065 8817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056066 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3325f9a7-d389-562e-ac1b-4eb26671f84b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056066 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492217 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186492973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492217 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186492988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492217 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186493004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492217 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492217 #edb/ref 1045 "Absolute Value Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492217 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186493004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492217 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492217 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492217 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "d762c7c1-b2fc-50f1-a9fc-7430b3a5a235" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492238 #edb/ref 1080 "-8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218